# Contact form configuration.
#
# Copy to .env for local work, and set the real values in the Vercel dashboard
# for production (Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables). .env is in
# .gitignore and .vercelignore: never committed, never deployed.
#
# NOTHING HERE REACHES THE BROWSER. api/contact.js reads these at request time
# and the response never echoes them, not even in an error message.

# ---- email delivery (required) --------------------------------------------
# Mail goes out through formsubmit.co, called server-to-server from
# api/contact.js. There is no API key: FormSubmit authenticates by the target
# itself, which is exactly why the target belongs here and not in the code.
#
# ACTIVATION IS REQUIRED AND IS A ONE-TIME MANUAL STEP.
# The first submission makes FormSubmit send a confirmation mail to this
# address. Nothing is delivered until the link in it is clicked. Until then the
# endpoint answers 502 and the form shows an error, which is correct: no mail
# has been sent.
#
# PREFER THE ALIAS. After activating, formsubmit.co issues a random string that
# delivers to the same inbox. Put that here instead of the address and the
# destination stops existing in any config at all:
#   FORMSUBMIT_TARGET=a1b2c3d4e5f6a7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6
FORMSUBMIT_TARGET=coverdesign.studio1@gmail.com

# ---- optional --------------------------------------------------------------
# The only origin allowed to POST the form. Defaults to the production host.
ALLOWED_ORIGIN=https://studiocoverdesign.com

# ---- reCAPTCHA v3 (optional, off until both halves are set) ----------------
# https://www.google.com/recaptcha/admin -> register the site, choose v3.
# The SECRET goes here. The SITE key goes in assets/js/forms-config.js.
# Unset means off, and the form still has origin checking, rate limiting, the
# honeypot, the timing gate, server-side validation and duplicate detection.
RECAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY=
RECAPTCHA_MIN_SCORE=0.5
